task (completed) {
  all questions should, by default, use the global scope
  - remove ./tags.toml
  - remove tags related statistics completely
  - remove all related code that is associated with tags, tags feature is deprecated

  Implemented:
  - Deleted ./tags.toml. Every question now searches the one global trunk
    corpus; there is no tag registry, tag scope, tag router, cross-tag
    fallback, tag filter, or tag completion.
  - chat.py
    - Removed --tag, the interactive Tag prompt, /tag, TagProfile, TagRoute,
      load_tags/get_tag/available_tags, tag filtering, auto routing, fallback,
      tag cache keys, and all tag fields in /status. load_chunks() now only
      loads the global corpus (or an explicit transcript set).
    - make_cache_key(), answer(), and chat_status_report() no longer take tag
      arguments or tag scope state.
  - app/chat_server.py
    - ChatState no longer has tag/tag_mode/resolved_tags/route/tag_profile
      fields. Every question uses state.chunks (the global corpus unless the
      user explicitly entered /article or /youtube transcript).
    - Removed /tag, the tag autocomplete kind, tag metadata in /api/state,
      and every tag-scoped answer/fallback branch.
    - Go, Rust, and PHP documentation support now keys off the programming
      language named in the question (detect_code_language), not a tag.
  - app/chat.html
    - Removed the tag status item, tag labels, /tag completion, tag-pinned
      language text, and the tag-based code-line-help check. Scope now shows
      "global corpus", or the active article/transcript.
  - youtube_video_learn.py: documented that ingestion always targets the one
    global corpus.

  Verified: chat.py and app/chat_server.py start with tags.toml absent;
  /api/state contains no tag fields and no /tag or /new command; the server
  loads all 11,406 trunks into the global corpus; /tag and /new now return the
  unknown-command response.
}

