task (completed) {
  perform the changes based on {directory_of_this_prompt}/../research/no_more_default_tag.html

  Implemented the recommended query-time auto-routing design (the global
  corpus and its BM25 index are never partitioned or rebuilt per question).

  chat.py
  - Added the `auto` scope mode (`AUTO_TAG`) and made it the default tag.
    `--tag <name>` and `/tag <name>` remain manual overrides.
  - Added a hybrid tag router. It scores every registry tag with four signals:
    IDF-weighted direct question/tag-name-and-description overlap, corpus
    co-occurrence between the question's rare anchors and the tag vocabulary
    (so "Tokyo"/"Nijo"/"wagyu" reach the japan tag even when the description
    does not repeat those words), tag-description coverage of the top
    question-matching chunks, and coverage of the top matching video titles.
  - A question that directly names a tag (for example "japan" or "rust") routes
    without a model call. Multi-topic questions where two tag names are equally
    strong use the global scope. Ambiguous questions ask qwen3:1.7b to choose
    among the top five lexical candidates using a few retrieved snippets as
    evidence; a low-support or malformed model answer falls back to the global
    scope instead of forcing a weak tag.
  - Routing is cached by normalized question, tag-registry version, corpus
    identity, active tag, and follow-up flag. Follow-ups keep the active
    resolved tag instead of rerouting on pronoun-heavy text.
  - Added `TagRoute`, `route_tags_for_question()`, `is_auto_tag()`, and tab
    completion/help text for `auto`.

  app/chat_server.py
  - `ChatState` now tracks `tag_mode`, `resolved_tags`, `route_source`, and
    route scores. `resolve_auto_scope()` runs before the first answer attempt
    and only changes metadata; the existing cross-tag fallback remains the
    safety net for a wrong route.
  - Manual tags, `/youtube transcript`, and `/article` scopes bypass routing.
    `/tag auto` restores auto mode and clears the current route; `/tag <name>`
    switches to a fixed manual tag.
  - `/status`, the status bar, and the session banner show the resolved scope
    as `auto → japan` or `auto → global`, and the benchmark stats include the
    chosen tags, route source, and top route scores.

  app/chat.html
  - Status and welcome text use the new `tag_label`, so auto routing is visible
    without hiding the effective tag.

  Verified routes on the current corpus include: nijo market → japan, 3am in
  Tokyo → japan, IDP → japan, wagyu → japan, binary search in rust → rust,
  Terence Tao → math, AI/software jobs → ai_and_coding, and an out-of-corpus
  question ("weather in Paris") → global.
}

